        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-10-21-000005",
        "note": "The Heath-Brown 1985 entry of this repository proves Vinogradov's three primes theorem, that every sufficiently large odd number is a sum of three primes, by Heath-Brown's route through Siegel-Walfisz and the binary Goldbach mean square. This entry proves more for three primes: the Hardy-Littlewood asymptotic with the constant C_3 for odd primes, Theorem D, by a separate circle method argument in LeanLab/PNTPort/Vinogradov and LeanLab/VanDerCorput1939, and builds Theorems B, C, E and F on it. Both entries share the Siegel-Walfisz theorem and the ported StrongPNT files; the three primes theorem itself also follows from theoremD_ternary here.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
